  "notes": "Source: official Cal Poly Pomona roadmap PDF 'Computer Science, B.S.: 120 units, 2021-2022 Academic Year' (Rev. 6/23/21, approved by the Office of Undergraduate Studies and General Education), hosted on cpp.edu: https://www.cpp.edu:443/academic-programs/academic-advising/tools/sheets-roadmaps/2021-2022/roadmaps/computer-science.pdf . Catalog year 2021-2022 is the actual year of the source roadmap. Transcription method: pdftotext -layout extraction of the official Fall/Spring term grid, manually verified row by row (courses, units, prereq notes, comments, semester totals). STALENESS CAVEAT: the university catalog (catalog.cpp.edu) now carries newer roadmap editions (2022-2023 through 2025-2026 'Program: Computer Science, B.S.: Roadmap 4-year (120 units)'), but that catalog host was unreachable from this collector, so this plan is built from the newest officially published roadmap PDF that could be retrieved (Rev. 6/23/21). The program has since evolved: the College of Science's 2026-2027 CS flowchart (https://cpp.edu/sci/advising-center/documents/2026-2027-cos-flowcharts-computer-science.pdf) lists 71 major units required (vs 67 in the 2024-2025 flowchart) and includes required courses absent from this roadmap (e.g. MAT 2250 Linear Algebra, CS 2610). Cross-checked course titles/units/prereqs against the roadmap PDF's own prereq notes; older quarter-era equivalents in those notes (CS 141/CS 130/CS 241/CS 311/CS 264/MAT 208/STA 326/MAT 132/MAT 1310/CS 128) were collapsed to their in-plan semester equivalents. Placement/eligibility conditions (C or better in MAT 1050/MAT 1060, MDTP/ALEKS score, 'eligibility for MAT 1140') are NOT course prerequisites and are documented here rather than in prereq fields. Grade conditions ('C or better'/'C- or better' on roadmap prereqs) are collapsed to plain course-code prereqs. Corequisites (BIO 1110L with BIO 1110; PHY 1510L with PHY 1510) are encoded as a prereq on the same-semester lecture. CS 4630 requires senior standing and CS 3750 requires lower-division GE completion (Area A, two Area B sub-areas, two Area D sub-areas) per the roadmap — standing/GE conditions, kept in notes. Graduation Writing Test milestone (take before 75 units) and the Year-4 'File an application to graduate' step are official milestones, not courses, and are noted here. GE slots and Major Elective slots are student-choice (choice:true); Major Elective picks come from the department's curriculum sheet; the two 1-unit elective slots carry the roadmap's recommendation (CS 4610 or CS 4620 or CS 4410).",
